    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005-sec-3",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "3 Definitions",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005#sec-3"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005.pdf, p.8",
      "values:originalText": "In this Act, unless the contrary intention appears:\nACMA means the Australian Communications and Media\nAuthority.\nACMA official means:\n(a) a member; or\n(b) an associate member; or\n(c) a member of the ACMA staff; or\n(d) a person whose services are made available to the ACMA\nunder subsection 55(1).\nACMA staff means the staff described in section 54.\nadditional functions, in relation to the ACMA, has the meaning\ngiven by section 11.\nappointer means:\n(a) for a member—the Governor-General; or\n(b) for an associate member—the Minister.\nassociate member means an associate member of the ACMA.\nauthorised disclosure information means:\n(a) information that was given in confidence to the ACMA in\nconnection with the performance of any of the ACMA’s\nfunctions or the exercise of any of its powers; or\n(b) information that was obtained by the ACMA as a result of\nthe exercise of any of its powers under:\n(i) Part 2, 5, 7, 8C, 9E or 13 of the Broadcasting Services\nAct 1992; or\n(ia) Part 3, 4 or 5 of the Interactive Gambling Act 2001; or\n\n\nPreliminary  Part 1\n\nSection 3\nAustralian Communications and Media Authority Act 2005\nCompilation date: 05/12/2025\n(ii) Chapter 3, 5 or 6 of the Radiocommunications Act 1992;\nor\n(iii) Part 3, 6, 21, 26 or 27 of the Telecommunications Act\n1997; or\n(iv) Schedule 3A to the Telecommunications Act 1997; or\n(v) Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection\nand Service Standards) Act 1999; or\n(c) information that was obtained by the ACMA as a result of\nthe exercise of powers under a provision that:\n(i) allows the ACMA or an ACMA official to require a\nperson to give information or to produce a document;\nand\n(ii) is a provision of an Act or a legislative instrument; and\n(iii) is not a provision described in paragraph (b); or\n(d) information that was given in confidence to the ACMA by a\ngovernment authority of a foreign country.\nbroadcasting, content and datacasting functions, in relation to the\nACMA, has the meaning given by section 10.\ncarriage service provider has the same meaning as in the\nTelecommunications Act 1997.\ncarrier has the same meaning as in the Telecommunications Act\n1997.\nChair means the Chair of the ACMA.\ncontract includes a deed.\nDeputy Chair means the Deputy Chair of the ACMA.\nDivision means a Division as described in section 46.\nends, in relation to a hearing, inquiry or investigation, has the\nmeaning given by section 4.",
      "skos:definition": "In this Act, unless the contrary intention appears:\nACMA means the Australian Communications and Media\nAuthority.\nACMA official means:\n(a) a member; or\n(b) an associate member; or\n(c) a member of the ACMA staff; or\n(d) a person whose services are made available to the ACMA\nunder subsection 55(1).\nACMA staff means the staff described in section 54.\nadditional functions, in relation to the ACMA, has the meaning\ngiven by section 11.\nappointer means:\n(a) for a member—the Governor-General; or\n(b) for an associate member—the Minister.\nassociate member means an associate member of the ACMA.\nauthorised disclosure information means:\n(a) information that was given in confidence to the ACMA in\nconnection with the performance of any of the ACMA’s\nfunctions or the exercise of any of its powers; or\n(b) information that was obtained by the ACMA as a result of\nthe exercise of any of its powers under:\n(i) Part 2, 5, 7, 8C, 9E or 13 of the Broadcasting Services\nAct 1992; or\n(ia) Part 3, 4 or 5 of the Interactive Gambling Act 2001; or\n\n\nPreliminary  Part 1\n\nSection 3\nAustralian Communications and Media Authority Act 2005\nCompilation date: 05/12/2025\n(ii) Chapter 3, 5 or 6 of the Radiocommunications Act 1992;\nor\n(iii) Part 3, 6, 21, 26 or 27 of the Telecommunications Act\n1997; or\n(iv) Schedule 3A to the Telecommunications Act 1997; or\n(v) Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection\nand Service Standards) Act 1999; or\n(c) information that was obtained by the ACMA as a result of\nthe exercise of powers under a provision that:\n(i) allows the ACMA or an ACMA official to require a\nperson to give information or to produce a document;\nand\n(ii) is a provision of an Act or a legislative instrument; and\n(iii) is not a provision described in paragraph (b); or\n(d) information that was given in confidence to the ACMA by a\ngovernment authority of a foreign country.\nbroadcasting, content and datacasting functions, in relation to the\nACMA, has the meaning given by section 10.\ncarriage service",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005-sec-3-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005-sec-3-logic-descriptionlogic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005-sec-3-logic-descriptionlogic-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "7f2fe08e81ddfc37cc8a6fb1e44ada9648f84b17e1e67b9473921dd3e0ba581c",
      "skos:note": "Definitions for ACMA terms"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005#sec-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "3 Definitions",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 8,
      "values:originalText": "In this Act, unless the contrary intention appears:\nACMA means the Australian Communications and Media\nAuthority.\nACMA official means:\n(a) a member; or\n(b) an associate member; or\n(c) a member of the ACMA staff; or\n(d) a person whose services are made available to the ACMA\nunder subsection 55(1).\nACMA staff means the staff described in section 54.\nadditional functions, in relation to the ACMA, has the meaning\ngiven by section 11.\nappointer means:\n(a) for a member—the Governor-General; or\n(b) for an associate member—the Minister.\nassociate member means an associate member of the ACMA.\nauthorised disclosure information means:\n(a) information that was given in confidence to the ACMA in\nconnection with the performance of any of the ACMA’s\nfunctions or the exercise of any of its powers; or\n(b) information that was obtained by the ACMA as a result of\nthe exercise of any of its powers under:\n(i) Part 2, 5, 7, 8C, 9E or 13 of the Broadcasting Services\nAct 1992; or\n(ia) Part 3, 4 or 5 of the Interactive Gambling Act 2001; or\n\n\nPreliminary  Part 1\n\nSection 3\nAustralian Communications and Media Authority Act 2005\nCompilation date: 05/12/2025\n(ii) Chapter 3, 5 or 6 of the Radiocommunications Act 1992;\nor\n(iii) Part 3, 6, 21, 26 or 27 of the Telecommunications Act\n1997; or\n(iv) Schedule 3A to the Telecommunications Act 1997; or\n(v) Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection\nand Service Standards) Act 1999; or\n(c) information that was obtained by the ACMA as a result of\nthe exercise of powers under a provision that:\n(i) allows the ACMA or an ACMA official to require a\nperson to give information or to produce a document;\nand\n(ii) is a provision of an Act or a legislative instrument; and\n(iii) is not a provision described in paragraph (b); or\n(d) information that was given in confidence to the ACMA by a\ngovernment authority of a foreign country.\nbroadcasting, content and datacasting functions, in relation to the\nACMA, has the meaning given by section 10.\ncarriage service provider has the same meaning as in the\nTelecommunications Act 1997.\ncarrier has the same meaning as in the Telecommunications Act\n1997.\nChair means the Chair of the ACMA.\ncontract includes a deed.\nDeputy Chair means the Deputy Chair of the ACMA.\nDivision means a Division as described in section 46.\nends, in relation to a hearing, inquiry or investigation, has the\nmeaning given by section 4."
    },
