      "dc:source": "australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005.pdf, p.13",
      "values:originalText": "(2) For the purposes of the finance law (within the meaning of the\nPublic Governance, Performance and Accountability Act 2013):\n(a) the ACMA is a listed entity; and\n(b) the Chair is the accountable authority of the ACMA; and\n(c) the ACMA officials are officials of the ACMA; and\n(d) the purposes of the ACMA include the functions of the\nACMA referred to in Division 2 of Part 2.",
      "skos:definition": "(2) For the purposes of the finance law (within the meaning of the\nPublic Governance, Performance and Accountability Act 2013):\n(a) the ACMA is a listed entity; and\n(b) the Chair is the accountable authority of the ACMA; and\n(c) the ACMA officials are officials of the ACMA; and\n(d) the purposes of the ACMA include the functions of the\nACMA referred to in Division 2 of Part 2.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005-sec-6"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005-sec-6-ss-2-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005-sec-6-ss-2-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005-sec-6-ss-2-logic-deontic-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005-sec-6-ss-2-logic-deontic-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "f9bf76e3965768aab9f34c074ecbb11810ea1f94b380d6b765e23551f9779f9d",
      "skos:note": "Establishes ACMA as a listed entity and defines its accountable authority."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005#sec-6-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "6(2) Establishment",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 13,
      "values:originalText": "(2) For the purposes of the finance law (within the meaning of the\nPublic Governance, Performance and Accountability Act 2013):\n(a) the ACMA is a listed entity; and\n(b) the Chair is the accountable authority of the ACMA; and\n(c) the ACMA officials are officials of the ACMA; and\n(d) the purposes of the ACMA include the functions of the\nACMA referred to in Division 2 of Part 2."
    },
