        "@id": "values:Agent"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005-sec-24-ss-4-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "MUST",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Must contain a statement",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(4) An associate member’s instrument of appointment...",
      "cml:conclusionText": "must contain a statement to the effect that..."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005-sec-25",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "25 Period of appointment for associate members",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005#sec-25"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005.pdf, p.26",
      "values:originalText": "Period specified in instrument of appointment\n(1) An associate member holds office for the period specified in his or\nher instrument of appointment. The period must not exceed 5\nyears.\nTotal periods of appointment must not exceed 10 years\n(2) A person can be appointed as an associate member more than once.\nHowever, a later appointment must not result in the sum of the\nperson’s periods of appointment exceeding 10 years.\nReduction if specified inquiry, investigation or hearing ends earlier\n(3) Despite subsection (1), if:\n\n\nACMA’s membership  Part 3\nMembership  Division 2\nSection 25\nAustralian Communications and Media Authority Act 2005\nCompilation date: 05/12/2025\n(a) an associate member’s instrument of appointment specifies\nthat the appointment relates to a specified inquiry,\ninvestigation or hearing; and\n(b) the inquiry, investigation or hearing ends before the end of\nthe period described in subsection (1);\nthe associate member holds office until the end of the inquiry,\ninvestigation or hearing.\nExtension to complete inquiry, investigation or hearing\n(4) Despite subsections (1) and (2), if an associate member is\nconducting, or is part of the panel conducting, an inquiry,\ninvestigation or hearing for the ACMA, the Minister may, by\nwriting, extend the associate member’s appointment until the end\nof the inquiry, investigation or hearing.\nFor 10 year rule, count membership and ABA and ACA\nmembership and associate membership\n(5) For the purposes of subsection (2), a period of appointment\nincludes (in addition to any periods when the person was an\nassociate member of the ACMA):\n(a) a period when the person was a member of the ACMA; or\n(b) a period before the commencement of section 6 when the\nperson was a member, or associate member, of the Australian\nBroadcasting Authority that was established by the\nBroadcasting Services Act 1992; or\n(c) a period:\n(i) starting on or after 1 July 1997; and\n(ii) ending before the commencement of section 6;\nwhen the person was a member, or associate member, of the\nbody corporate that was continued in existence by section 14\nof the Australian Communications Authority Act 1997.",
      "skos:definition": "Period specified in instrument of appointment\n(1) An associate member holds office for the period specified in his or\nher instrument of appointment. The period must not exceed 5\nyears.\nTotal periods of appointment must not exceed 10 years\n(2) A person can be appointed as an associate member more than once.\nHowever, a later appointment must not result in the sum of the\nperson’s periods of appointment exceeding 10 years.\nReduction if specified inquiry, investigation or hearing ends earlier\n(3) Despite subsection (1), if:\n\n\nACMA’s membership  Part 3\nMembership  Division 2\nSection 25\nAustralian Communications and Media Authority Act 2005\nCompilation date: 05/12/2025\n(a) an associate member’s instrument of appointment specifies\nthat the appointment relates to a specified inquiry,\ninvestigation or hearing; and\n(b) the inquiry, investigation or hearing ends before the end of\nthe period described in subsection (1);\nthe associate member holds office until the end of the inquiry,\ninvestigation or hearing.\nExtension to complete inquiry, investigation or hearing\n(4) Despite subsections (1) and (2), if an associate member is\nconducting, or is part of the panel conducting, an inquiry,\ninvestigation or hearing for the ACMA, the Minister may, by\nwriting, extend the associate member’s appointment until the end\nof the inquiry, investigation or hearing.\nFor 10 year rule, count membership and ABA and ACA\nmembership and associate membership\n(5) For the purposes of subsection (2), a period of appointment\nincludes (in addition to any periods when the person was an\nassociate member of the ACMA):\n(a) a period when the person was a member of the ACMA; or\n(b) a period before the commencement of section 6 when the\nperson was a member, or associate member, of the Australian\nBroadcasting Authority that was established by the\nBroadcasting Services Act 1992; or\n(c) a period:\n(i) starting on or after 1 July 1997; and\n(ii) ending before the commencement of section 6;\nwhen the person was a member, or",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005-sec-25-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005-sec-25-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005-sec-25-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005-sec-25-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005-sec-25-ss-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "8877884c0af3e64e1eeb12113acf797684597b928937b3acdf4f89d5bbdf1af0"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005#sec-25",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "25 Period of appointment for associate members",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 26,
      "values:originalText": "Period specified in instrument of appointment\n(1) An associate member holds office for the period specified in his or\nher instrument of appointment. The period must not exceed 5\nyears.\nTotal periods of appointment must not exceed 10 years\n(2) A person can be appointed as an associate member more than once.\nHowever, a later appointment must not result in the sum of the\nperson’s periods of appointment exceeding 10 years.\nReduction if specified inquiry, investigation or hearing ends earlier\n(3) Despite subsection (1), if:\n\n\nACMA’s membership  Part 3\nMembership  Division 2\nSection 25\nAustralian Communications and Media Authority Act 2005\nCompilation date: 05/12/2025\n(a) an associate member’s instrument of appointment specifies\nthat the appointment relates to a specified inquiry,\ninvestigation or hearing; and\n(b) the inquiry, investigation or hearing ends before the end of\nthe period described in subsection (1);\nthe associate member holds office until the end of the inquiry,\ninvestigation or hearing.\nExtension to complete inquiry, investigation or hearing\n(4) Despite subsections (1) and (2), if an associate member is\nconducting, or is part of the panel conducting, an inquiry,\ninvestigation or hearing for the ACMA, the Minister may, by\nwriting, extend the associate member’s appointment until the end\nof the inquiry, investigation or hearing.\nFor 10 year rule, count membership and ABA and ACA\nmembership and associate membership\n(5) For the purposes of subsection (2), a period of appointment\nincludes (in addition to any periods when the person was an\nassociate member of the ACMA):\n(a) a period when the person was a member of the ACMA; or\n(b) a period before the commencement of section 6 when the\nperson was a member, or associate member, of the Australian\nBroadcasting Authority that was established by the\nBroadcasting Services Act 1992; or\n(c) a period:\n(i) starting on or after 1 July 1997; and\n(ii) ending before the commencement of section 6;\nwhen the person was a member, or associate member, of the\nbody corporate that was continued in existence by section 14\nof the Australian Communications Authority Act 1997."
    },
