    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005-sec-25-ss-4",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "25(4) Period of appointment for associate members",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005#sec-25-ss-4"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005.pdf, p.26",
      "values:originalText": "(4) Despite subsections (1) and (2), if an associate member is\nconducting, or is part of the panel conducting, an inquiry,\ninvestigation or hearing for the ACMA, the Minister may, by\nwriting, extend the associate member’s appointment until the end\nof the inquiry, investigation or hearing.\nFor 10 year rule, count membership and ABA and ACA\nmembership and associate membership",
      "skos:definition": "(4) Despite subsections (1) and (2), if an associate member is\nconducting, or is part of the panel conducting, an inquiry,\ninvestigation or hearing for the ACMA, the Minister may, by\nwriting, extend the associate member’s appointment until the end\nof the inquiry, investigation or hearing.\nFor 10 year rule, count membership and ABA and ACA\nmembership and associate membership",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005-sec-25"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005-sec-25-ss-4-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005-sec-25-ss-4-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "cf74ef5bad6fd606035bd5fa0f91f0ff6b2be33577d886012969c0ff3484af0c",
      "skos:note": "Extend associate member's appointment until end of inquiry, investigation or hearing."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005#sec-25-ss-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "25(4) Period of appointment for associate members",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 26,
      "values:originalText": "(4) Despite subsections (1) and (2), if an associate member is\nconducting, or is part of the panel conducting, an inquiry,\ninvestigation or hearing for the ACMA, the Minister may, by\nwriting, extend the associate member’s appointment until the end\nof the inquiry, investigation or hearing.\nFor 10 year rule, count membership and ABA and ACA\nmembership and associate membership"
    },
