    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005-sec-29",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "29 Disclosure of interests",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005#sec-29"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005.pdf, p.29",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A disclosure by a member or associate member under section 29 of\nthe Public Governance, Performance and Accountability Act 2013\n(which deals with the duty to disclose interests) must be made to\nthe Minister.\n(2) Subsection (1) applies in addition to any rules made for the\npurposes of that section.\n(3) For the purposes of this Act and the Public Governance,\nPerformance and Accountability Act 2013, the member or\nassociate member is taken not to have complied with section 29 of\nthat Act if he or she does not comply with subsection (1) of this\nsection.\n(4) The Chair must inform the Minister if the members of the ACMA\nagree, in accordance with any rules made for the purposes of\nsection 29 of the Public Governance, Performance and\nAccountability Act 2013, to a member or associate member doing",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A disclosure by a member or associate member under section 29 of\nthe Public Governance, Performance and Accountability Act 2013\n(which deals with the duty to disclose interests) must be made to\nthe Minister.\n(2) Subsection (1) applies in addition to any rules made for the\npurposes of that section.\n(3) For the purposes of this Act and the Public Governance,\nPerformance and Accountability Act 2013, the member or\nassociate member is taken not to have complied with section 29 of\nthat Act if he or she does not comply with subsection (1) of this\nsection.\n(4) The Chair must inform the Minister if the members of the ACMA\nagree, in accordance with any rules made for the purposes of\nsection 29 of the Public Governance, Performance and\nAccountability Act 2013, to a member or associate member doing",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005-sec-29-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005-sec-29-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005-sec-29-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005-sec-29-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "96c9e2cbeb1ac1fa47700e287450bedfbfb3242dc6252573857f5c55b6b85aa3"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005#sec-29",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "29 Disclosure of interests",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 29,
      "values:originalText": "(1) A disclosure by a member or associate member under section 29 of\nthe Public Governance, Performance and Accountability Act 2013\n(which deals with the duty to disclose interests) must be made to\nthe Minister.\n(2) Subsection (1) applies in addition to any rules made for the\npurposes of that section.\n(3) For the purposes of this Act and the Public Governance,\nPerformance and Accountability Act 2013, the member or\nassociate member is taken not to have complied with section 29 of\nthat Act if he or she does not comply with subsection (1) of this\nsection.\n(4) The Chair must inform the Minister if the members of the ACMA\nagree, in accordance with any rules made for the purposes of\nsection 29 of the Public Governance, Performance and\nAccountability Act 2013, to a member or associate member doing"
    },
