      "cof:pageNumber": 34,
      "values:originalText": "(1) At a meeting of the ACMA, a quorum is constituted by a majority\nof the members.\n(2) However, if:\n(a) rules made for the purposes of section 29 of the Public\nGovernance, Performance and Accountability Act 2013\nprevent a member from participating in the deliberations, or\ndecisions, of the ACMA with respect to a particular matter;\nand\n(b) when the member leaves the meeting concerned there is no\nlonger a quorum present;\nthe remaining members at the meeting constitute a quorum for the\npurpose of any deliberation or decision at that meeting with respect\nto that matter."
    },
