      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005.pdf, p.34",
      "values:originalText": "(1) At a meeting of the ACMA, a question is decided by a majority of\nthe votes of the following people present and voting:\n(a) the members; and\n\n\nDecision-making and delegation by ACMA  Part 4\nMeetings  Division 1\nSection 42\nAustralian Communications and Media Authority Act 2005\nCompilation date: 05/12/2025\n(b) if the question relates to a matter connected with an inquiry,\ninvestigation, hearing or other matter specified in the\ninstruments of appointment of 1 or more associate\nmembers—that associate member, or each of those associate\nmembers.\n(2) The person presiding at a meeting has a deliberative vote and, if\nnecessary, also a casting vote.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) At a meeting of the ACMA, a question is decided by a majority of\nthe votes of the following people present and voting:\n(a) the members; and\n\n\nDecision-making and delegation by ACMA  Part 4\nMeetings  Division 1\nSection 42\nAustralian Communications and Media Authority Act 2005\nCompilation date: 05/12/2025\n(b) if the question relates to a matter connected with an inquiry,\ninvestigation, hearing or other matter specified in the\ninstruments of appointment of 1 or more associate\nmembers—that associate member, or each of those associate\nmembers.\n(2) The person presiding at a meeting has a deliberative vote and, if\nnecessary, also a casting vote.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005-sec-41-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005-sec-41-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "49709545d2e977ffa0de645fcfbc94d43f80c667131f801b56c5af991c3b088f"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005#sec-41",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "41 Voting at meetings etc.",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 34,
      "values:originalText": "(1) At a meeting of the ACMA, a question is decided by a majority of\nthe votes of the following people present and voting:\n(a) the members; and\n\n\nDecision-making and delegation by ACMA  Part 4\nMeetings  Division 1\nSection 42\nAustralian Communications and Media Authority Act 2005\nCompilation date: 05/12/2025\n(b) if the question relates to a matter connected with an inquiry,\ninvestigation, hearing or other matter specified in the\ninstruments of appointment of 1 or more associate\nmembers—that associate member, or each of those associate\nmembers.\n(2) The person presiding at a meeting has a deliberative vote and, if\nnecessary, also a casting vote."
    },
