          "@id": "concept:australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005-sec-47-ss-2-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005-sec-47-ss-2-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "cc32292012f123da4b0332823d7fbffe181581f1cef9d5aec266aa14fc885bb9",
      "skos:note": "Rules for meetings of a Division"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005#sec-47-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "47(2) Meetings of a Division",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 38,
      "values:originalText": "(2) Subject to subsection (3), a Division may determine its own rules\nrelating to meetings, including (for example) rules about the\nfollowing:\n\n\nDecision-making and delegation by ACMA  Part 4\nDivisions  Division 3\nSection 48\nAustralian Communications and Media Authority Act 2005\nCompilation date: 05/12/2025\n(a) calling of meetings;\n(b) notice of meetings;\n(c) presiding at meetings;\n(d) how decisions are made at meetings, including quorum\nrequirements and voting entitlements and procedures.\nThe rules that the Division determines displace the rules that would\notherwise apply under subsection (1), to the extent of any\ninconsistency."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005-sec-47-ss-2-norm",
