      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005-sec-47-ss-3",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "47(3) Meetings of a Division",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005#sec-47-ss-3"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005.pdf, p.38",
      "values:originalText": "(3) A Division cannot:\n(a) determine rules that purport to exclude the operation of, or\nthat are inconsistent with, rules made for the purposes of\nsection 29 of the Public Governance, Performance and\nAccountability Act 2013, or any provision of this Act (other\nthan subsection (1) of this section); or\n(b) determine rules under which an associate member would be\nallowed to vote on a question that does not relate to a matter\nconnected with an inquiry, investigation, hearing or other\nmatter specified in the instrument of appointment of the\nassociate member.\nNote:\nSection 33B of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901 provides for\nparticipation in meetings by telephone etc.",
      "skos:definition": "(3) A Division cannot:\n(a) determine rules that purport to exclude the operation of, or\nthat are inconsistent with, rules made for the purposes of\nsection 29 of the Public Governance, Performance and\nAccountability Act 2013, or any provision of this Act (other\nthan subsection (1) of this section); or\n(b) determine rules under which an associate member would be\nallowed to vote on a question that does not relate to a matter\nconnected with an inquiry, investigation, hearing or other\nmatter specified in the instrument of appointment of the\nassociate member.\nNote:\nSection 33B of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901 provides for\nparticipation in meetings by telephone etc.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005-sec-47"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005-sec-47-ss-3-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005-sec-47-ss-3-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "ff65ca203f63f060064f36ee714487a5d5b2e8943e3a0af8fee127a19aa7f1ff",
      "skos:note": "Cannot determine rules excluding or inconsistent with other rules."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005#sec-47-ss-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "47(3) Meetings of a Division",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 38,
      "values:originalText": "(3) A Division cannot:\n(a) determine rules that purport to exclude the operation of, or\nthat are inconsistent with, rules made for the purposes of\nsection 29 of the Public Governance, Performance and\nAccountability Act 2013, or any provision of this Act (other\nthan subsection (1) of this section); or\n(b) determine rules under which an associate member would be\nallowed to vote on a question that does not relate to a matter\nconnected with an inquiry, investigation, hearing or other\nmatter specified in the instrument of appointment of the\nassociate member.\nNote:\nSection 33B of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901 provides for\nparticipation in meetings by telephone etc."
    },
