    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005-sec-50",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "50 Delegations by ACMA to a Division",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005#sec-50"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005.pdf, p.41",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The ACMA may, by writing, delegate to a Division any or all of\nthe ACMA’s functions and powers so far as they relate to the kinds\nof matters the Division can deal with.\n(2) A certificate:\n(a) stating any matter with respect to the performance of a\ndelegated function or exercise of a delegated power; and\n(b) signed by:\n(i) a member in the Division; or\n(ii) an associate member who participated, or could have\nparticipated, in the making of the Division’s decision to\nperform the delegated function or exercise the delegated\npower;\nis prima facie evidence of the matter.\n(3) A document purporting to be a certificate mentioned in\nsubsection (2) is taken to be such a certificate and to have been\nduly given unless the contrary is established.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The ACMA may, by writing, delegate to a Division any or all of\nthe ACMA’s functions and powers so far as they relate to the kinds\nof matters the Division can deal with.\n(2) A certificate:\n(a) stating any matter with respect to the performance of a\ndelegated function or exercise of a delegated power; and\n(b) signed by:\n(i) a member in the Division; or\n(ii) an associate member who participated, or could have\nparticipated, in the making of the Division’s decision to\nperform the delegated function or exercise the delegated\npower;\nis prima facie evidence of the matter.\n(3) A document purporting to be a certificate mentioned in\nsubsection (2) is taken to be such a certificate and to have been\nduly given unless the contrary is established.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005-sec-50-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005-sec-50-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005-sec-50-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "74551a817b92d48015ff011eb7805762d4d6420ffe7fc6b3635d45d1a72c5151"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005#sec-50",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "50 Delegations by ACMA to a Division",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 41,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The ACMA may, by writing, delegate to a Division any or all of\nthe ACMA’s functions and powers so far as they relate to the kinds\nof matters the Division can deal with.\n(2) A certificate:\n(a) stating any matter with respect to the performance of a\ndelegated function or exercise of a delegated power; and\n(b) signed by:\n(i) a member in the Division; or\n(ii) an associate member who participated, or could have\nparticipated, in the making of the Division’s decision to\nperform the delegated function or exercise the delegated\npower;\nis prima facie evidence of the matter.\n(3) A document purporting to be a certificate mentioned in\nsubsection (2) is taken to be such a certificate and to have been\nduly given unless the contrary is established."
    },
