    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005-sec-51",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "51 Delegations by ACMA to others",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005#sec-51"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005.pdf, p.41",
      "values:originalText": "(1) Subject to subsection (2) and section 53, the ACMA may, by\nwriting, delegate any or all of its functions and powers to:\n(a) a member; or\n(b) an associate member, if the delegated function or power\nrelates to a matter connected with an inquiry, investigation,\nhearing or other matter specified in the associate member’s\ninstrument of appointment; or\n(c) a member of the ACMA staff; or\n(d) a person whose services are made available to the ACMA\nunder subsection 55(1).",
      "skos:definition": "(1) Subject to subsection (2) and section 53, the ACMA may, by\nwriting, delegate any or all of its functions and powers to:\n(a) a member; or\n(b) an associate member, if the delegated function or power\nrelates to a matter connected with an inquiry, investigation,\nhearing or other matter specified in the associate member’s\ninstrument of appointment; or\n(c) a member of the ACMA staff; or\n(d) a person whose services are made available to the ACMA\nunder subsection 55(1).",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005-sec-51-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "8c1e75f5b0d73ef09295d36982f686c509a412e1d1ef6f0b26fe1eec55a50b9f",
      "skos:note": "Delegations of functions and powers by ACMA to others"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005#sec-51",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "51 Delegations by ACMA to others",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 41,
      "values:originalText": "(1) Subject to subsection (2) and section 53, the ACMA may, by\nwriting, delegate any or all of its functions and powers to:\n(a) a member; or\n(b) an associate member, if the delegated function or power\nrelates to a matter connected with an inquiry, investigation,\nhearing or other matter specified in the associate member’s\ninstrument of appointment; or\n(c) a member of the ACMA staff; or\n(d) a person whose services are made available to the ACMA\nunder subsection 55(1)."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005-sec-51-norm",
