    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005-sec-53",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "53 Limit on powers delegable to persons other than Divisions",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005#sec-53"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005.pdf, p.44",
      "values:originalText": "(2) Sections 51 and 52 do not apply to a power to do any of the\nfollowing under the Broadcasting Services Act 1992:\n(a) cancel or suspend licences;\n(b) decide that a person is not suitable to be allocated or to\ncontinue to hold a licence;\n(c) impose, vary or revoke a condition on a licence (other than a\ntiming condition on a temporary community broadcasting\nlicence);\n(d) determine, vary or revoke a program standard;\n(g) prepare or vary licence area plans under section 26 of that\nAct;\n(h) give an opinion under section 21 or 74 of that Act;\n(i) approve or refuse to approve temporary breaches under\nsection 67 of that Act;\n(j) make, vary or revoke a determination under section 103L of\nthat Act;\n(ja) make, vary or revoke a determination about regulated\ntelevision devices under subsection 130ZZI(2) or (3) of that\nAct;\n(jb) make, vary or revoke an instrument about primary user\ninterfaces under subsection 130ZZL(3) of that Act;\n\n\nDecision-making and delegation by ACMA  Part 4\nDelegations  Division 4\nSection 53\nAustralian Communications and Media Authority Act 2005\nCompilation date: 05/12/2025\n(jc) determine, vary or revoke guidelines about regulated\ntelevision devices under section 130ZZM of that Act;\n(l) refer a matter to the Director of Public Prosecutions;\n(m) initiate a hearing.\n(3) Subsection (2) does not limit the generality of subsection 51(2) or\n52(1A).\nNote:\nSubsections 51(2) and 52(1A) are additional limitations on the\ndelegation of powers in relation to instruments.",
      "skos:definition": "(2) Sections 51 and 52 do not apply to a power to do any of the\nfollowing under the Broadcasting Services Act 1992:\n(a) cancel or suspend licences;\n(b) decide that a person is not suitable to be allocated or to\ncontinue to hold a licence;\n(c) impose, vary or revoke a condition on a licence (other than a\ntiming condition on a temporary community broadcasting\nlicence);\n(d) determine, vary or revoke a program standard;\n(g) prepare or vary licence area plans under section 26 of that\nAct;\n(h) give an opinion under section 21 or 74 of that Act;\n(i) approve or refuse to approve temporary breaches under\nsection 67 of that Act;\n(j) make, vary or revoke a determination under section 103L of\nthat Act;\n(ja) make, vary or revoke a determination about regulated\ntelevision devices under subsection 130ZZI(2) or (3) of that\nAct;\n(jb) make, vary or revoke an instrument about primary user\ninterfaces under subsection 130ZZL(3) of that Act;\n\n\nDecision-making and delegation by ACMA  Part 4\nDelegations  Division 4\nSection 53\nAustralian Communications and Media Authority Act 2005\nCompilation date: 05/12/2025\n(jc) determine, vary or revoke guidelines about regulated\ntelevision devices under section 130ZZM of that Act;\n(l) refer a matter to the Director of Public Prosecutions;\n(m) initiate a hearing.\n(3) Subsection (2) does not limit the generality of subsection 51(2) or\n52(1A).\nNote:\nSubsections 51(2) and 52(1A) are additional limitations on the\ndelegation of powers in relation to instruments.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005-sec-53-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005-sec-53-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "c6c840100764206c4bcf074501f13ac5296e981398022082c5f1d4141247a342"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005#sec-53",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "53 Limit on powers delegable to persons other than Divisions",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 44,
      "values:originalText": "(2) Sections 51 and 52 do not apply to a power to do any of the\nfollowing under the Broadcasting Services Act 1992:\n(a) cancel or suspend licences;\n(b) decide that a person is not suitable to be allocated or to\ncontinue to hold a licence;\n(c) impose, vary or revoke a condition on a licence (other than a\ntiming condition on a temporary community broadcasting\nlicence);\n(d) determine, vary or revoke a program standard;\n(g) prepare or vary licence area plans under section 26 of that\nAct;\n(h) give an opinion under section 21 or 74 of that Act;\n(i) approve or refuse to approve temporary breaches under\nsection 67 of that Act;\n(j) make, vary or revoke a determination under section 103L of\nthat Act;\n(ja) make, vary or revoke a determination about regulated\ntelevision devices under subsection 130ZZI(2) or (3) of that\nAct;\n(jb) make, vary or revoke an instrument about primary user\ninterfaces under subsection 130ZZL(3) of that Act;\n\n\nDecision-making and delegation by ACMA  Part 4\nDelegations  Division 4\nSection 53\nAustralian Communications and Media Authority Act 2005\nCompilation date: 05/12/2025\n(jc) determine, vary or revoke guidelines about regulated\ntelevision devices under section 130ZZM of that Act;\n(l) refer a matter to the Director of Public Prosecutions;\n(m) initiate a hearing.\n(3) Subsection (2) does not limit the generality of subsection 51(2) or\n52(1A).\nNote:\nSubsections 51(2) and 52(1A) are additional limitations on the\ndelegation of powers in relation to instruments."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005-sec-53-ss-2",
