    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005-sec-59b",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "59B Disclosure to public servants for advising their Ministers",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005#sec-59b"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005.pdf, p.52",
      "values:originalText": "(1) For the purpose of advising the Minister, an ACMA official may\ndisclose authorised disclosure information to:\n(a) the Secretary of the Department; or\n(b) an APS employee in the Department who is authorised, in\nwriting, by the Secretary of the Department for the purposes\nof this subsection.\n(1A) For the purpose of advising the Minister, an ACMA official must,\nif requested to do so by:\n(a) the Secretary of the Department; or\n(b) an APS employee in the Department who is authorised, in\nwriting, by the Secretary of the Department for the purposes\nof this subsection;\ndisclose authorised disclosure information to the Secretary of the\nDepartment or the APS employee, as the case requires.\n(2) For the purpose of advising a Minister administering a particular\nprovision of an Act, an ACMA official may disclose authorised\ndisclosure information relating to a matter arising under that\nprovision to:\n\n\nDisclosure of information  Part 7A\n\nSection 59C\nAustralian Communications and Media Authority Act 2005\nCompilation date: 05/12/2025\n(a) the Secretary of the Department that is administered by that\nMinister; or\n(b) an APS employee in that Department who is authorised, in\nwriting, by the Secretary of that Department for the purposes\nof this subsection.\n(3) Subsection (2) does not limit subsection (1) or (1A).",
      "skos:definition": "(1) For the purpose of advising the Minister, an ACMA official may\ndisclose authorised disclosure information to:\n(a) the Secretary of the Department; or\n(b) an APS employee in the Department who is authorised, in\nwriting, by the Secretary of the Department for the purposes\nof this subsection.\n(1A) For the purpose of advising the Minister, an ACMA official must,\nif requested to do so by:\n(a) the Secretary of the Department; or\n(b) an APS employee in the Department who is authorised, in\nwriting, by the Secretary of the Department for the purposes\nof this subsection;\ndisclose authorised disclosure information to the Secretary of the\nDepartment or the APS employee, as the case requires.\n(2) For the purpose of advising a Minister administering a particular\nprovision of an Act, an ACMA official may disclose authorised\ndisclosure information relating to a matter arising under that\nprovision to:\n\n\nDisclosure of information  Part 7A\n\nSection 59C\nAustralian Communications and Media Authority Act 2005\nCompilation date: 05/12/2025\n(a) the Secretary of the Department that is administered by that\nMinister; or\n(b) an APS employee in that Department who is authorised, in\nwriting, by the Secretary of that Department for the purposes\nof this subsection.\n(3) Subsection (2) does not limit subsection (1) or (1A).",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005-sec-59b-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005-sec-59b-ss-1a"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005-sec-59b-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005-sec-59b-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "18942cee38e2881c54114e13a2015f8366a01586739f9229436b7f7922cff117"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005#sec-59b",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "59B Disclosure to public servants for advising their Ministers",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 52,
      "values:originalText": "(1) For the purpose of advising the Minister, an ACMA official may\ndisclose authorised disclosure information to:\n(a) the Secretary of the Department; or\n(b) an APS employee in the Department who is authorised, in\nwriting, by the Secretary of the Department for the purposes\nof this subsection.\n(1A) For the purpose of advising the Minister, an ACMA official must,\nif requested to do so by:\n(a) the Secretary of the Department; or\n(b) an APS employee in the Department who is authorised, in\nwriting, by the Secretary of the Department for the purposes\nof this subsection;\ndisclose authorised disclosure information to the Secretary of the\nDepartment or the APS employee, as the case requires.\n(2) For the purpose of advising a Minister administering a particular\nprovision of an Act, an ACMA official may disclose authorised\ndisclosure information relating to a matter arising under that\nprovision to:\n\n\nDisclosure of information  Part 7A\n\nSection 59C\nAustralian Communications and Media Authority Act 2005\nCompilation date: 05/12/2025\n(a) the Secretary of the Department that is administered by that\nMinister; or\n(b) an APS employee in that Department who is authorised, in\nwriting, by the Secretary of that Department for the purposes\nof this subsection.\n(3) Subsection (2) does not limit subsection (1) or (1A)."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005-sec-59b-ss-1",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "59B(1) Disclosure to public servants for advising their Ministers",
