      "dc:source": "australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005.pdf, p.52",
      "values:originalText": "(1A) For the purpose of advising the Minister, an ACMA official must,\nif requested to do so by:\n(a) the Secretary of the Department; or\n(b) an APS employee in the Department who is authorised, in\nwriting, by the Secretary of the Department for the purposes\nof this subsection;\ndisclose authorised disclosure information to the Secretary of the\nDepartment or the APS employee, as the case requires.",
      "skos:definition": "(1A) For the purpose of advising the Minister, an ACMA official must,\nif requested to do so by:\n(a) the Secretary of the Department; or\n(b) an APS employee in the Department who is authorised, in\nwriting, by the Secretary of the Department for the purposes\nof this subsection;\ndisclose authorised disclosure information to the Secretary of the\nDepartment or the APS employee, as the case requires.",
