        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "84acef5d80e953b9ea201985eb2633bb8f5e74343bc900d6d8df885bf23b860f",
      "skos:note": "Disclosure of information for advising Ministers"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005#sec-59b-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "59B(2) Disclosure to public servants for advising their Ministers",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 52,
      "values:originalText": "(2) For the purpose of advising a Minister administering a particular\nprovision of an Act, an ACMA official may disclose authorised\ndisclosure information relating to a matter arising under that\nprovision to:\n\n\nDisclosure of information  Part 7A\n\nSection 59C\nAustralian Communications and Media Authority Act 2005\nCompilation date: 05/12/2025\n(a) the Secretary of the Department that is administered by that\nMinister; or\n(b) an APS employee in that Department who is authorised, in\nwriting, by the Secretary of that Department for the purposes\nof this subsection."
    },
