    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005-sec-59d",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "59D Disclosure to certain authorities",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005#sec-59d"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005.pdf, p.53",
      "values:originalText": "(1) An ACMA official authorised by the Chair, in writing, for the\npurposes of this section may disclose authorised disclosure\ninformation to any of the following authorities if the Chair is\nsatisfied that the information will enable or assist the authority to\nperform or exercise any of its functions or powers:\n(a) the Australian Bureau of Statistics;\n(b) the Australian Competition and Consumer Commission;\n(c) the Australian Prudential Regulation Authority;\n(d) the Australian Securities and Investments Commission;\n(e) the Commissioner of Taxation;",
      "skos:definition": "(1) An ACMA official authorised by the Chair, in writing, for the\npurposes of this section may disclose authorised disclosure\ninformation to any of the following authorities if the Chair is\nsatisfied that the information will enable or assist the authority to\nperform or exercise any of its functions or powers:\n(a) the Australian Bureau of Statistics;\n(b) the Australian Competition and Consumer Commission;\n(c) the Australian Prudential Regulation Authority;\n(d) the Australian Securities and Investments Commission;\n(e) the Commissioner of Taxation;",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005-sec-59d-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005-sec-59d-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005-sec-59d-logic-alleninterval-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005-sec-59d-logic-ltl-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005-sec-59d-logic-diffusion-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005-sec-59d-logic-cogai-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "5f4a6c67a83b1a7109729277d7f655d0e9cf1b6e1343852d086640e41e2b1c17",
      "skos:note": "Disclosure of information to certain authorities with Chair's satisfaction"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005#sec-59d",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "59D Disclosure to certain authorities",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 53,
      "values:originalText": "(1) An ACMA official authorised by the Chair, in writing, for the\npurposes of this section may disclose authorised disclosure\ninformation to any of the following authorities if the Chair is\nsatisfied that the information will enable or assist the authority to\nperform or exercise any of its functions or powers:\n(a) the Australian Bureau of Statistics;\n(b) the Australian Competition and Consumer Commission;\n(c) the Australian Prudential Regulation Authority;\n(d) the Australian Securities and Investments Commission;\n(e) the Commissioner of Taxation;"
    },
