    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005-sec-60",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "60 Charges relating to ACMA’s expenses",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005#sec-60"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005.pdf, p.61",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The ACMA may, by written instrument, make determinations\nfixing charges for:\n(a) services provided by the ACMA; and\n(b) any matter in relation to which expenses are incurred by the\nACMA under:\n(i) this Act; or\n(ii) the Telecommunications Act 1997; or\n(iii) the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and\nService Standards) Act 1999; or\n(iv) the Radiocommunications Act 1992; or\n(v) the Broadcasting Services Act 1992; or\n(vi) an instrument made under an Act referred to in\nsubparagraph (ii), (iii), (iv) or (v);\nand specifying the persons by whom, and the times when, the\ncharges are payable.\n(2) A charge fixed under subsection (1) must not be such as to amount\nto taxation.\n(3) For the purposes of recovering all or part of the ACMA’s expenses\nrelating to the performance of its functions under\nparagraph 11(1)(a) or (b), the ACMA may charge a person an\namount that has been:\n(a) agreed with the person; or\n(b) worked out under an agreement with the person.\nNote 1:\nParagraph 11(1)(a) is about the ACMA preparing to provide for the\nmanagement of electronic addressing, and paragraph 11(1)(b) is about\nthe ACMA providing for the management of electronic addressing.\nNote 2:\nSubsection (3) lets the ACMA charge a consenting person for things\ndone by the ACMA in performing those functions, even though the",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The ACMA may, by written instrument, make determinations\nfixing charges for:\n(a) services provided by the ACMA; and\n(b) any matter in relation to which expenses are incurred by the\nACMA under:\n(i) this Act; or\n(ii) the Telecommunications Act 1997; or\n(iii) the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and\nService Standards) Act 1999; or\n(iv) the Radiocommunications Act 1992; or\n(v) the Broadcasting Services Act 1992; or\n(vi) an instrument made under an Act referred to in\nsubparagraph (ii), (iii), (iv) or (v);\nand specifying the persons by whom, and the times when, the\ncharges are payable.\n(2) A charge fixed under subsection (1) must not be such as to amount\nto taxation.\n(3) For the purposes of recovering all or part of the ACMA’s expenses\nrelating to the performance of its functions under\nparagraph 11(1)(a) or (b), the ACMA may charge a person an\namount that has been:\n(a) agreed with the person; or\n(b) worked out under an agreement with the person.\nNote 1:\nParagraph 11(1)(a) is about the ACMA preparing to provide for the\nmanagement of electronic addressing, and paragraph 11(1)(b) is about\nthe ACMA providing for the management of electronic addressing.\nNote 2:\nSubsection (3) lets the ACMA charge a consenting person for things\ndone by the ACMA in performing those functions, even though the",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005-sec-60-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005-sec-60-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005-sec-60-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "9ed8b965b87f3e08106df484728bd3837341290255fd0efe8b7df28baabf51c2"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005#sec-60",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "60 Charges relating to ACMA’s expenses",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 61,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The ACMA may, by written instrument, make determinations\nfixing charges for:\n(a) services provided by the ACMA; and\n(b) any matter in relation to which expenses are incurred by the\nACMA under:\n(i) this Act; or\n(ii) the Telecommunications Act 1997; or\n(iii) the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and\nService Standards) Act 1999; or\n(iv) the Radiocommunications Act 1992; or\n(v) the Broadcasting Services Act 1992; or\n(vi) an instrument made under an Act referred to in\nsubparagraph (ii), (iii), (iv) or (v);\nand specifying the persons by whom, and the times when, the\ncharges are payable.\n(2) A charge fixed under subsection (1) must not be such as to amount\nto taxation.\n(3) For the purposes of recovering all or part of the ACMA’s expenses\nrelating to the performance of its functions under\nparagraph 11(1)(a) or (b), the ACMA may charge a person an\namount that has been:\n(a) agreed with the person; or\n(b) worked out under an agreement with the person.\nNote 1:\nParagraph 11(1)(a) is about the ACMA preparing to provide for the\nmanagement of electronic addressing, and paragraph 11(1)(b) is about\nthe ACMA providing for the management of electronic addressing.\nNote 2:\nSubsection (3) lets the ACMA charge a consenting person for things\ndone by the ACMA in performing those functions, even though the"
    },
