    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005-sec-60-ss-3",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "60(3) Charges relating to ACMA’s expenses",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005#sec-60-ss-3"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005.pdf, p.61",
      "values:originalText": "(3) For the purposes of recovering all or part of the ACMA’s expenses\nrelating to the performance of its functions under\nparagraph 11(1)(a) or (b), the ACMA may charge a person an\namount that has been:\n(a) agreed with the person; or\n(b) worked out under an agreement with the person.\nNote 1:\nParagraph 11(1)(a) is about the ACMA preparing to provide for the\nmanagement of electronic addressing, and paragraph 11(1)(b) is about\nthe ACMA providing for the management of electronic addressing.\nNote 2:\nSubsection (3) lets the ACMA charge a consenting person for things\ndone by the ACMA in performing those functions, even though the",
      "skos:definition": "(3) For the purposes of recovering all or part of the ACMA’s expenses\nrelating to the performance of its functions under\nparagraph 11(1)(a) or (b), the ACMA may charge a person an\namount that has been:\n(a) agreed with the person; or\n(b) worked out under an agreement with the person.\nNote 1:\nParagraph 11(1)(a) is about the ACMA preparing to provide for the\nmanagement of electronic addressing, and paragraph 11(1)(b) is about\nthe ACMA providing for the management of electronic addressing.\nNote 2:\nSubsection (3) lets the ACMA charge a consenting person for things\ndone by the ACMA in performing those functions, even though the",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005-sec-60"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005-sec-60-ss-3-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005-sec-60-ss-3-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "8913a39e05ebf1b29606a07e3f145fbe8c1e69939503380640e891481aa24410",
      "skos:note": "ACMA may charge a person for expenses related to its functions."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005#sec-60-ss-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "60(3) Charges relating to ACMA’s expenses",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 61,
      "values:originalText": "(3) For the purposes of recovering all or part of the ACMA’s expenses\nrelating to the performance of its functions under\nparagraph 11(1)(a) or (b), the ACMA may charge a person an\namount that has been:\n(a) agreed with the person; or\n(b) worked out under an agreement with the person.\nNote 1:\nParagraph 11(1)(a) is about the ACMA preparing to provide for the\nmanagement of electronic addressing, and paragraph 11(1)(b) is about\nthe ACMA providing for the management of electronic addressing.\nNote 2:\nSubsection (3) lets the ACMA charge a consenting person for things\ndone by the ACMA in performing those functions, even though the"
    },
