    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005-sec-62",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "62 ACMA’s expenses include related Commonwealth expenses",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005#sec-62"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005.pdf, p.62",
      "values:originalText": "A reference in section 60, or a provision of another Act, to an\nexpense (however described) incurred by the ACMA in relation to\na thing, includes a reference to an expense incurred by the\nCommonwealth in relation to the thing.",
      "skos:definition": "A reference in section 60, or a provision of another Act, to an\nexpense (however described) incurred by the ACMA in relation to\na thing, includes a reference to an expense incurred by the\nCommonwealth in relation to the thing.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005-sec-62-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005-sec-62-logic-descriptionlogic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "c4117d0085b344528047fa666016eaa009e961d9f96a93599f1c55b248878ed6",
      "skos:note": "ACMA's expenses include related Commonwealth expenses"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005#sec-62",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "62 ACMA’s expenses include related Commonwealth expenses",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 62,
      "values:originalText": "A reference in section 60, or a provision of another Act, to an\nexpense (however described) incurred by the ACMA in relation to\na thing, includes a reference to an expense incurred by the\nCommonwealth in relation to the thing."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005-sec-62-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005-sec-62"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:Agent"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005-sec-62-logic-descriptionlogic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:DescriptionLogic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "includes",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Classifies the relation between ACMA's expenses and related Commonwealth expenses",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::dl",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "ACMA's expenses include...",
      "cml:conclusionText": "...related Commonwealth expenses"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005-sec-62a",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "62A Proceedings in the name of the ACMA",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005#sec-62a"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005.pdf, p.62",
      "values:originalText": "(1) Proceedings brought by the Commonwealth in relation to the\nfunctions or powers of the ACMA may be brought in the name of\nthe ACMA.\nNote:\nThis subsection does not authorise ACMA to bring proceedings\nagainst the Commonwealth: see also subsection 62B(2).\n(2) Proceedings brought against the Commonwealth in relation to the\nfunctions or powers of the ACMA may be brought against the\nCommonwealth in the name of the ACMA.\n\n\nOther matters  Part 8\n\nSection 62B\nAustralian Communications and Media Authority Act 2005\nCompilation date: 05/12/2025\n62B  Decisions relating to the Commonwealth etc.\n(1) The fact that the ACMA does not have a legal identity separate\nfrom the Commonwealth does not affect the performance of the\nACMA’s functions in making, or the exercise of the ACMA’s\npowers to make, decisions relating to:\n(a) the Commonwealth; or\n(b) any authority of the Commonwealth that is not a body\ncorporate.\n(2) This section does not apply to decisions relating to bringing\nproceedings against the Commonwealth or such an authority.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) Proceedings brought by the Commonwealth in relation to the\nfunctions or powers of the ACMA may be brought in the name of\nthe ACMA.\nNote:\nThis subsection does not authorise ACMA to bring proceedings\nagainst the Commonwealth: see also subsection 62B(2).\n(2) Proceedings brought against the Commonwealth in relation to the\nfunctions or powers of the ACMA may be brought against the\nCommonwealth in the name of the ACMA.\n\n\nOther matters  Part 8\n\nSection 62B\nAustralian Communications and Media Authority Act 2005\nCompilation date: 05/12/2025\n62B  Decisions relating to the Commonwealth etc.\n(1) The fact that the ACMA does not have a legal identity separate\nfrom the Commonwealth does not affect the performance of the\nACMA’s functions in making, or the exercise of the ACMA’s\npowers to make, decisions relating to:\n(a) the Commonwealth; or\n(b) any authority of the Commonwealth that is not a body\ncorporate.\n(2) This section does not apply to decisions relating to bringing\nproceedings against the Commonwealth or such an authority.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005-sec-62a-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005-sec-62a-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005-sec-62a-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005-sec-62a-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "78a9e041e5ee2c9c7434518c15d455527b91eba9df3995cba6bc154187f6c609"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005#sec-62a",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "62A Proceedings in the name of the ACMA",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 62,
      "values:originalText": "(1) Proceedings brought by the Commonwealth in relation to the\nfunctions or powers of the ACMA may be brought in the name of\nthe ACMA.\nNote:\nThis subsection does not authorise ACMA to bring proceedings\nagainst the Commonwealth: see also subsection 62B(2).\n(2) Proceedings brought against the Commonwealth in relation to the\nfunctions or powers of the ACMA may be brought against the\nCommonwealth in the name of the ACMA.\n\n\nOther matters  Part 8\n\nSection 62B\nAustralian Communications and Media Authority Act 2005\nCompilation date: 05/12/2025\n62B  Decisions relating to the Commonwealth etc.\n(1) The fact that the ACMA does not have a legal identity separate\nfrom the Commonwealth does not affect the performance of the\nACMA’s functions in making, or the exercise of the ACMA’s\npowers to make, decisions relating to:\n(a) the Commonwealth; or\n(b) any authority of the Commonwealth that is not a body\ncorporate.\n(2) This section does not apply to decisions relating to bringing\nproceedings against the Commonwealth or such an authority."
    },
