    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005-sec-62a-ss-1",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "62A(1) Proceedings in the name of the ACMA",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005#sec-62a-ss-1"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005.pdf, p.62",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The fact that the ACMA does not have a legal identity separate\nfrom the Commonwealth does not affect the performance of the\nACMA’s functions in making, or the exercise of the ACMA’s\npowers to make, decisions relating to:\n(a) the Commonwealth; or\n(b) any authority of the Commonwealth that is not a body\ncorporate.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The fact that the ACMA does not have a legal identity separate\nfrom the Commonwealth does not affect the performance of the\nACMA’s functions in making, or the exercise of the ACMA’s\npowers to make, decisions relating to:\n(a) the Commonwealth; or\n(b) any authority of the Commonwealth that is not a body\ncorporate.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005-sec-62a"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005-sec-62a-ss-1-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-communications-and-media-authority-act-2005-sec-62a-ss-1-logic-deontic-1"
        },
